cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or the associated paper, please cite it using these metadata.
title: "Simulating the finite-resolution HHL spectral filter with tensor networks and qudits"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mata Ali
    given-names: Alejandro
    email: alejandro.mata.ali@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DOKOS-TAYOS/Tensor_Networks_HHL_algorithm"
url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.05290"
abstract: >-
  This software formulates HHL with qudits and simulates its finite-resolution
  spectral filter using tensor networks. It evaluates the joint postselected
  branch conditioned on ancilla success and a zero-valued phase register,
  studies behaviour both on and off the exact spectral grid, and treats the
  success probability separately. It is intended for validation and
  benchmarking of this finite-resolution procedure.
